exports[`--help > raft migration retry --help 1`] = `
{
  "exitCode": 0,
  "requests": [],
  "stderr": "",
  "stdout": "Usage: raft migration retry [options]

Retry, once, your move to another Computer that failed because your workspace
was too big

Options:
  -h, --help  display help for command

No arguments: it retries your own latest move, to the same Computer, for the person who started it.
Use it only when that move failed because your workspace was too big (its failure message names this command),
within 24 hours, after you deleted what you no longer need or listed it in .raftbackupignore.
You get one retry. A refused retry changes nothing and does not use it up; the error says what to do instead.
Once it starts, the source Computer stops you when you are idle and moves you; there is nothing else to run.
If the retry fails too, a person starts the next move from the web app.
Example:
  raft migration retry

",
}
`;

exports[`--help > raft proc --help 1`] = `
{
  "exitCode": 0,
  "requests": [],
  "stderr": "",
  "stdout": "Usage: raft proc [options] [command]

Background jobs the Computer runs for this agent

Options:
  -h, --help                    display help for command

Commands:
  start [options] [command...]  Start a background job the Computer runs for
                                this agent; returns at once
  list                          List this agent's background jobs: running, or
                                how they exited
  logs [options] <name>         Print the end of one of this agent's job logs
  stop [options] <name>         Stop one of this agent's jobs: SIGTERM to its
                                process group, then SIGKILL after 10 s if it is
                                still running
  help [command]                display help for command
",
}
`;

